<h2 id="company-and-account">1. The company and account covered</h2>

<p>This authorization is between the customer or authorized account representative accepting it (&quot;you&quot;) and the transportation booking company identified on this screen (&quot;Company&quot;). It covers the customer or business account and payment methods you designate. The Company&#x27;s legal name and billing identity, the account covered, and the version of this authorization are retained with your acceptance. For Koast&#x27;s own operating business, the Company is Krujim Inc, doing business as Koast.</p>

<p>This authorization applies to transportation bookings and their related authorized charges. It does not authorize purchases unrelated to transportation or charges by every company that uses the same software.</p>

<h2 id="authorized-requests">2. Who may request service</h2>

<p>You authorize the Company to arrange, create, modify and administer transportation that you request, that a booker you designate requests within their authority, or that follows recurring or other standing service instructions you have separately given and that the Company has accepted. Requests may be made through the available app, website, phone, email, messaging, or an agreed business booking channel. Company staff may enter and manage those reservations on your behalf.</p>

<p>Your authorized bookers and any agreed limits are recorded with your account. Service may be requested for you, your passengers, guests, family members, employees or other travelers within those instructions. A staff-created reservation must be supported by an authorized request or an applicable standing instruction. Staff access to Dispatch alone does not establish your approval.</p>

<p>You do not need to click a separate confirmation or re-enter your card for each reservation that falls within this authorization. The Company still needs to accept the reservation and provide its confirmation.</p>

<h2 id="services">3. Services covered</h2>

<p>Subject to availability, lawful operation and your selected scope, this authorization can cover:</p>

<ul>
<li>One-way transfers, airport transfers, round trips and separately identified return legs.</li>
<li>Hourly/as-directed transportation and event transportation.</li>
<li>The vehicle classes offered by the Company, including sedans, SUVs and quoted van, Sprinter and bus services.</li>
<li>Multiple passengers, ordered additional stops, return stops and requested itinerary changes.</li>
<li>Additional service time or distance, and garage-based departure/return or positioning when that billing basis is included in the agreed framework.</li>
<li>Requested vehicle/service add-ons, extra services and pass-through expenses identified in the agreed pricing and ride-policy schedule.</li>
<li>Business, negotiated or account pricing that you or your authorized representative has agreed to.</li>
</ul>

<p>A service being listed here does not guarantee its availability or activate a feature that the Company has not offered. Quote-only services remain subject to an agreed quote or another specifically agreed pricing arrangement; their inclusion here does not turn them into an unspecified automatic fare.</p>

<h2 id="pricing-policies">4. Pricing and ride-policy schedule</h2>

<p>When you accept this authorization, the Company provides the pricing and ride-policy schedule it covers. That schedule must identify the applicable service categories, how the price is determined, what may vary, and how the applicable policy is selected for a ride. It may include different rules for transfers, hourly service, events, vehicle classes, airports, return legs and custom-quoted services.</p>

<p>The agreed framework identifies, as applicable:</p>

<ul>
<li>Quoted, negotiated or formula-based fares; included services; applicable currency; required charges and permitted separately stated government charges.</li>
<li>Hourly minimums, included distance, billing start/end points, garage or positioning basis, time precision and additional time or mileage rates.</li>
<li>Waiting allowances, the starting point of each waiting clock, airport/flight treatment, intermediate-stop waiting and the rate/precision for extra waiting.</li>
<li>Cancellation deadlines, calculation of cancellation charges and refunds, no-show conditions and any required contact or timing evidence.</li>
<li>Add-ons, quantities, unit prices, quoted extras, eligible pass-through expenses and their evidence requirements.</li>
<li>Any gratuity or service charge you have selected or expressly agreed to, together with its amount or calculation method.</li>
<li>Any customer-selected spending, booker, service, geographic or other limits.</li>
</ul>

<p>Your scope may cover all listed service categories. Spending limits can be offered as customer controls; this authorization does not impose a universal dollar cap. An authorization without a customer-selected cap still requires an authorized service request and a determinable charge under the agreed framework.</p>

<p>For each reservation, the Company identifies the applicable service, itinerary, price or agreed calculation basis, selected ride policy, and included services in the booking record and confirmation. Each leg retains its own applicable terms. The confirmation records how the previously agreed framework applies; receiving it or failing to cancel is not a substitute for agreement to a new rule outside that framework.</p>

<h2 id="payment-methods">5. Saving and automatically charging your payment method</h2>

<p>You authorize the Company to save your designated payment method through its payment provider for future transportation payments, display an eligible saved method to you for future bookings, and initiate one or more payments without requiring your participation in each payment attempt. Payments are made as requested services occur or as otherwise provided by your agreed booking/billing arrangement; they are not a subscription or a fixed recurring charge merely because your card is saved.</p>

<p>This permission covers the agreed fare and supported adjustments for the authorized service, plus cancellation, no-show, waiting, additional time/distance, add-ons, expenses, taxes and agreed gratuity/service charges only where the applicable agreed terms authorize them. Charges must follow those terms, any recorded limits and the service or event giving rise to the charge.</p>

<p>The booking/billing arrangement states charging timing, including completion charges or any specifically agreed deposit, prepayment or cancellation/no-show collection. The Company provides a receipt or appropriate payment record. The presence of a deposit field, manual amount adjustment, custom line or auto-collection setting does not independently authorize a charge.</p>

<p>Where another payment method is agreed for a ride, the Company must reconcile that payment and any pending payment request before charging the same obligation to a saved card. An alternate-payment balance may be collected from a saved card only if that fallback was expressly included in your authorization. This agreement does not authorize the Company to pull money through Zelle, Venmo, a bank account or another payment service without the separate permission and process applicable to that method.</p>

<p>You may designate which saved method is primary and whether any other method you designate may be used as a fallback. The Company may not use another person&#x27;s payment method merely because it is accessible in the software. Your bank or payment provider may still require authentication or decline a payment; in that event, the Company may ask you to complete a secure payment step.</p>

<h2 id="changes">6. Changes and additional charges</h2>

<p>Changes requested by you or an authorized booker may be administered without a fresh confirmation click where their price and conditions are already covered by your agreed framework and limits. An operational substitution that does not add charges or worsen your agreed service terms does not by itself require a new payment authorization.</p>

<p>A manual fare adjustment or custom charge must have an agreed service/pricing basis. The Company cannot use it to add an unrelated, undisclosed or unsupported fee. An optional gratuity cannot be increased at staff discretion under this authorization. Claimed damage, cleaning, penalties or similar exceptional charges require a previously agreed lawful basis, supporting evidence and appropriate review; this paragraph does not establish a new fee schedule for them.</p>

<p>Where a proposed booking or change falls outside your authorization, the Company requests approval for that exception or invites you to approve an expanded standing authorization. Posting a new policy online, sending a confirmation, retaining your card, or your silence does not by itself expand the agreed scope. Later policy or rate-setting changes do not retroactively reprice an accepted ride.</p>

<h2 id="other-providers">7. Other transportation providers</h2>

<p>The Company may arrange fulfillment by a qualified affiliated or independent transportation provider where that arrangement is covered by your booking agreement. A different chauffeur or fulfilling provider does not by itself change the company authorized to charge you or remove the agreed ride protections.</p>

<p>If a different company becomes your contracting or charging company, this authorization does not automatically transfer to it. That company must establish the appropriate agreement and payment authorization with you. An operator using the software does not receive access to another operator&#x27;s saved cards or standing authorizations merely by providing a ride.</p>

<h2 id="withdrawal">8. Review, changes and withdrawal</h2>

<p>You can request a copy of this authorization and the terms associated with a reservation, update your authorized bookers or limits, change a designated payment method, or withdraw permission for future bookings/automatic payments by contacting the Company using the support details in your confirmation, or through available account controls.</p>

<p>Withdrawal takes effect for future activity after the Company receives and can verify the request. It does not itself cancel a reservation, erase an amount validly owed or authorize a new charge. The Company explains how any already authorized or outstanding service/payment will be handled under the applicable agreement and law. You retain mandatory consumer, payment-dispute and privacy rights.</p>

<p>The Company retains the acceptance record, the version accepted, relevant service requests, booking terms and payment records for their applicable operational and legal purposes, as described in its privacy notice. Customer permissions for marketing messages, optional recording, device tracking or cross-operator profile sharing remain separate.</p>
